{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01PzRk16yThDtPAaGjwnYieE","type":"tool_result","content":"\"\"\"Check, before it is quoted, the rate function for the size of the largest\ncomponent of G(n, c/n) in the form O'Connell (1998) gives it, as restated by\nPuhalskii (2005, Ann. Probab. 33, remark after Corollary 2.5; his (2.13)-(2.14)):\n\n    K_rho(u) = u log(rho u / (1 - e^{-rho u})) - rho u^2 / 2,\n    L_c(u)   = (1 - u) log(1 - u) + (c - log c) u - c u^2 / 2,\n    I_c^beta(u) = k K_c(u) + L_c(k u)   for u in [x_k, x_{k-1}],  x_0 = 1,\n    x_k the solution of x / (1 - e^{-c x}) = 1 - k x.\n\nTwo things are checked numerically (item 01 of loop0011, 2026-11-01):\n(1) I vanishes at the law-of-large-numbers point u* = 1 - rho, 1 - u* = e^{-c u*};\n(2) inf over u <= 1/2 of I is positive iff c > 2 ln 2, i.e. iff u* > 1/2.\nNothing here is a theorem of ours; it is a sanity check of a quotation.\n\"\"\"\nimport math\n\ndef K(rho, u):\n    if u == 0: return 0.0\n    return u * math.log(rho * u / (1 - math.exp(-rho * u))) - rho * u * u / 2\n\ndef L(c, u):\n    return (1 - u) * math.log(1 - u) + (c - math.log(c)) * u - c * u * u / 2 if u < 1 else (c - math.log(c)) - c / 2\n\ndef x_k(c, k):\n    # solve x/(1-e^{-cx}) = 1 - k x on (0, 1/k) by bisection; LHS - RHS increasing\n    lo, hi = 1e-12, 1.0 / k - 1e-12\n    f = lambda x: x / (1 - math.exp(-c * x)) - (1 - k * x)\n    if f(lo) > 0: return 0.0\n    for _ in range(200):\n        mid = (lo + hi) / 2\n        if f(mid) > 0: hi = mid\n        else: lo = mid\n    return (lo + hi) / 2\n\ndef I(c, u):\n    if u <= 0: return L(c, max(0.0, 1 - 1 / c))\n    k = 1\n    while True:\n        xk, xk1 = x_k(c, k), (1.0 if k == 1 else x_k(c, k - 1))\n        if xk <= u <= xk1 + 1e-15:\n            return k * K(c, u) + L(c, k * u)\n        k += 1\n        if k > 10000: return float('nan')\n\ndef giant(c):\n    if c <= 1: return 0.0\n    lo, hi = 1e-12, 1 - 1e-12\n    for _ in range(200):\n        mid = (lo + hi) / 2\n        if 1 - mid - math.exp(-c * mid) > 0: lo = mid\n        else: hi = mid\n    return (lo + hi) / 2\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n  print(\"c  u*=giant  I(u*)  x_1  I(1/2)  min_{u<=1/2} I  c>2ln2\")\n  for c in [1.2, 1.386, 1.4, 1.5, 2.0, 2.772, 3.0, 4.0, 4.98, 6.0, 8.0, 10.0]:\n      us = giant(c)\n      grid = [i / 2000 for i in range(1, 1001)]\n      m = min(I(c, u) for u in grid)\n      print(f\"{c:5.3f} {us:.4f} {I(c, us):+.2e} {x_k(c,1):.4f} {I(c,0.5):+.5f} {m:+.5f} {c > 2*math.log(2)}\")\n----\nc  u*=giant  I(u*)  x_1  I(1/2)  min_{u<=1/2} I  c>2ln2\n1.200 0.3137 -9.71e-17 0.1103 +0.00479 +0.00000 False\n1.386 0.4998 +5.55e-17 0.1831 +0.00000 +0.00000 False\n1.400 0.5110 -5.55e-17 0.1877 +0.00002 +0.00002 True\n1.500 0.5828 +1.39e-16 0.2183 +0.00153 +0.00153 True\n2.000 0.7968 +0.00e+00 0.3219 +0.03619 +0.03619 True\n2.772 0.9225 +1.11e-16 0.4018 +0.14374 +0.14374 True\n3.000 0.9405 -2.22e-16 0.4163 +0.18309 +0.18309 True\n4.000 0.9802 -4.44e-16 0.4561 +0.37956 +0.37956 True\n4.980 0.9929 +0.00e+00 0.4754 +0.59513 +0.59513 True\n6.000 0.9975 +6.66e-16 0.4861 +0.83239 +0.83239 True\n8.000 0.9997 -4.44e-16 0.4952 +1.31610 +1.31610 True\n10.000 1.0000 +4.44e-16 0.4983 +1.81023 +1.81023 True","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"cba2c2ba-5816-43aa-8494-5f91637f4c84","uuid":"21667b15-ecd9-44df-89cf-8660f5841a95","timestamp":"2026-11-01T16:40:41.317Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"\"\"\"Check, before it is quoted, the rate function for the size of the largest\ncomponent of G(n, c/n) in the form O'Connell (1998) gives it, as restated by\nPuhalskii (2005, Ann. Probab. 33, remark after Corollary 2.5; his (2.13)-(2.14)):\n\n    K_rho(u) = u log(rho u / (1 - e^{-rho u})) - rho u^2 / 2,\n    L_c(u)   = (1 - u) log(1 - u) + (c - log c) u - c u^2 / 2,\n    I_c^beta(u) = k K_c(u) + L_c(k u)   for u in [x_k, x_{k-1}],  x_0 = 1,\n    x_k the solution of x / (1 - e^{-c x}) = 1 - k x.\n\nTwo things are checked numerically (item 01 of lo