 working precision is `60 + 0.6 · N(1−p)^{N−1}` digits (94 at `N = 400`,","+  `c′ = 2`). The item's 60 digits would have failed at `N = 400`, `c′ = 2`","+  (`C_400 ≈ e^{−54}`, 24 digits of cancellation, and the terms carry the","+  rounding of 400 further subtractions).","+* `log_prob_partition(λ, N, p)`: `N!/(Π λ_i! Π_s m_s!) · Π C_{λ_i} · (1−p)^{(N² − Σ λ_i²)/2}`.","+  With `a(s) = log C_s − log s! − (s²/2) log(1−p)` this is","+  `N! (1−p)^{N²/2} Π_s e^{m_s a(s)}/m_s!`, i.e. the exponential formula:","+  the sum over all partitions is `[x^N] exp(Σ_s e^{a(s)} x^s)`.","+* `log_prob_rel(N, p, M)`: that coefficient with the sum cut at `s ≤ M`,","+  the `O(N · M)` recursion the item asked for (over the multiplicity of the","+  largest part rather than the component of the first vertex; the two are","+  the same table). `N = 400` in under a second once `C_j` is known.","+* `log_prob_bip(N, p, t)`: the sum over the partitions with a sub-multiset","+  summing to `t`, by a **memoised recursion over the part sizes** (largest","+  first) carrying the set of achievable sub-sums as a bitset, with two","+  closures: a branch whose bitset already contains `t` is closed by the","+  coefficient table (every completion qualifies; this is what makes it","+  fast), and a part larger than `t` closes a branch at zero. The bitset is","+  reduced to the bits in `[t − r, t]` before memoisation (`r` the vertices","+  left to place), which is what keeps the state count polynomial-looking in","+  practice: 20,863 states at `N = 60` (0.1 s), 115,065 at 80 (0.5 s),","+  514,206 at 100 (2.5 s), 1,980,380 at 120 (18 s). The item's plain","+  enumeration of the 966,467 partitions of 60 was never needed; `N = 160`","+  would be about 8 M states and was not run.","+","+All sums are of positive terms and are done in floating-point logs; only","+the connectedness recursion needs multiple precision.","+","+### 5.2 The finite table at the pilot cells","+","+Largest `k` with each bound below `1` and below `0.01`; `β*(c)·n` the","+asymptotic threshold of the pair count; the pilot's observed minimum","+pathwidth where the cell is proved (`n = 60`) and the solver's smallest","+lower bound where it is not (`n = 120`, 13 graphs per cell, none proved","+at `c ≥ 4`, 3 of 13 at `c = 3`; `reports/scratch/gnp_pilot/results.csv`).","+","+| `n` | `c` | pair `< 1` | pair `< .01` | xpair `< 1` | xpair `< .01` | **sep `< 1`** | **sep `< .01`** | relax `< 1` | relax `< .01` | `β*n` | graphs | exact | min pw | min LB |","+|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|","+| 60 | 3 | 1 | — | 1 | 0 | **3** | **1** | 3 | 1 | 0.5 | 136 | 136 | 5 | — |","+| 60 | 4 | 5 | 3 | 5 | 3 | **6** | **4** | 6 | 4 | 3.7 | 136 | 136 | 8 | — |","+| 60 | 6 | 11 | 11 | 12 | 11 | **12** | **11** | 12 | 11 | 10.2 | 134 | 134 | 16 | — |","+| 60 | 8 | 17 | 17 | 18 | 17 | **18** | **17** | 18 | 17 | 15.8 | 132 | 132 | 20 | — |","+| 60 | 10 | 23 | 21 | 23 | 21 | **23** | **22** | 23 | 22 | 20.2 | 133 | 133 | 25 | — |","+| 120 | 3 | 1 | 1 | 2 | 1 | **5** | **4** | 5 | 4 | 1.0 | 13 | 3 | 11 | 12 |","+| 120 | 4 | 9 | 7 | 9 | 7 | **11** | **10** | 11 | 10 | 7.4 | 13 | 0 | — | 17 |","+| 120 | 6 | 21 | 21 | 22 | 21 | **24** | **22** | 24 | 22 | 20.5 | 13 | 0 | — | 25 |","+| 120 | 8 | 33 | 33 | 34 | 33 | **34** | **33** | 34 | 33 | 31.5 | 13 | 0 | — | 34 |","+| 120 | 10 | 43 | 41 | 43 | 42 | **44** | **42** | 44 | 42 | 40.5 | 13 | 0 | — | 41 |","+","+(`inner.csv`, `floors.csv`.) Read it by the 0.01 column, where the pair","+count's parity rounding (`B_pair` depends on `k` only through `t`) does","+not confuse the count:","+","+* **At `c ≥ 6` the separator floor is the pair floor or one stack above","+  it** in all six cells (`+0, +0, +1` at `n = 60`; `+1, +0, +1` at 120),","+  and never above the exact-size pair floor by more than one. That is the","+  kill criterion, met (§5.5).","+* **At `c = 3–4` it is two to three stacks above**: `−1 → 1` and `3 → 4`","+  at `n = 60`; `1 → 4` and `7 → 10` at `n 